## Contract Examples

### Cross-Chain Token Transfer
```rust
// Example contract using IBC transfers
#[entry_point]
pub fn execute(
    deps: DepsMut,
    env: Env,
    info: MessageInfo,
    msg: ExecuteMsg,
) -> Result<Response, ContractError> {
    match msg {
        ExecuteMsg::TransferToChain { 
            recipient, 
            amount, 
            destination_chain 
        } => {
            let ibc_msg = IbcMsg::Transfer {
                channel_id: "channel-0".to_string(),
                to_address: recipient,
                amount: amount,
                timeout: env.block.time.plus_seconds(3600),
            };
            
            Ok(Response::new()
                .add_message(ibc_msg)
                .add_attribute("action", "cross_chain_transfer"))
        }
    }
}
```

### Cross-Chain Contract Call
```rust
#[entry_point]
pub fn execute(
    deps: DepsMut,
    env: Env,
    info: MessageInfo,
    msg: ExecuteMsg,
) -> Result<Response, ContractError> {
    match msg {
        ExecuteMsg::CallRemoteContract { 
            channel_id, 
            remote_contract, 
            call_data 
        } => {
            let packet_data = CrossChainCallData {
                contract_address: remote_contract,
                msg: call_data,
                sender: info.sender.to_string(),
            };
            
            let ibc_msg = IbcMsg::SendPacket {
                channel_id,
                data: to_binary(&packet_data)?,
                timeout: env.block.time.plus_seconds(600),
            };
            
            Ok(Response::new()
                .add_message(ibc_msg)
                .add_attribute("action", "cross_chain_call"))
        }
    }
}
```

## Migration Strategy

### Phase 1: Non-Breaking Enhancement
1. Add IBC adapters alongside existing nil implementations
2. Make IBC dependencies optional in depinject
3. Maintain backward compatibility

### Phase 2: Full Integration
1. Update all contracts to use IBC features
2. Add comprehensive testing
3. Update documentation

### Phase 3: Advanced Features
1. Implement IBC callbacks
2. Add cross-chain state synchronization
3. Enable multi-chain workflows

